The Rust workspace under rust/ (including the rusty-claude-cli crate that builds
the `neuron` binary), the Python porting workspace under src/ and tests/, and
the parity documents were imported from Claw Code and have since been modified.
The Claw Code copyright and permission notice is reproduced in LICENSE and must
be kept in all copies or substantial portions of the software. See
docs/PROVENANCE.md for the code lineage. Fixes ported from later Claw Code
commits (fork point about 00d0eb6, reviewed up to 51cfca1) are listed with their
upstream commit SHAs under "Later ports from Claw Code" in docs/PROVENANCE.md.

Full-screen UI (neuron-tui)
---------------------------

The full-screen terminal UI under ui/neuron-tui, released as the neuron-tui
binaries, is derived from the Freebuff CLI (its cli/ package, and 31 files of its
common/src vendored under ui/neuron-tui/src/vendor/common) at
https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff commit 545e04d, and has since been
modified: Codebuff's services, ads, billing and telemetry were removed. It is
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose full text is in
ui/neuron-tui/LICENSE. Files changed from the originals start with a
"Derived from Codebuff/Freebuff (Apache-2.0); modified for Neuron" notice. The
Freebuff NOTICE file reads:

    Codebuff
    Copyright 2025 Codebuff

    This product includes software developed for the Codebuff project.

The neuron-tui binary is compiled with Bun and contains the Bun runtime and npm
packages, among them OpenTUI and React. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md on every release
lists them with their licenses and reproduces ui/neuron-tui/LICENSE and NOTICE.

Shared client (neuron-client), used by the desktop and mobile apps
------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of ui/neuron-client are ported from Freebuff's common/src/desktop-cloud
at https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff commit 0dc95cb, Copyright Codebuff,
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in ui/neuron-tui/LICENSE; the
Freebuff NOTICE above applies):

  src/threads.ts, test/threads.test.ts
      from threads.ts and threads.test.ts: the thread digest and its group,
      step count and status line. Modified: zod schemas replaced by plain
      types; cloud kinds, funding, git, pull requests and the panel layout
      removed; the digest is built from a Neuron session.
  src/remote.ts (reconnectDelay and the silence watchdog)
      after run-stream.ts (CloudRunReader): a silence watchdog, jittered
      backoff and a stall report, rewritten for a WebSocket transport.

Each of these files says so at the top.

